{"seq":13,"trial_id":"shared-bot-scope-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-14T14:48:06.798Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"1ffbb50f28c6b09a7fdec0575667bab76735463d15888954e4cea8c3c0bae544","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files (four North digests and two Central ones). Two ticket numbers are tagged to Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md, 5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025: drivers checking in at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched the SMS gateway routing that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift went through fine. There was also an action item to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nSome notes:\n• The two numbers look alike (4492 vs 4419), but the notes describe them as different problems (SMS bay assignments vs barcode scanners), so I've listed them as separate tickets. I can't confirm from the notes that one isn't a typo of the other.\n• The 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23/2026 renewal note both mention QFL but give no ticket numbers.\n• Tickets #4409 and #4412 and FR-882 in Moss's Central notes belong to Central accounts, not QFL. Marcus's \"Quarendon Freightways\" note is about a different company that isn't a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
